# Rottenmouth Viper's rulings: the opponent "loses 4 life the appropriate number of times", all at once with their other
# choices. Each 4 is its own loss of life (CR 119.3), one simultaneous event (CR 101.4, 603.2c) with one life change for
# each: Bloodthirsty Conqueror's "whenever an opponent loses life, you gain that much life" triggers once for each 4, not
# once for an 8. Bot1 casts the Conqueror from Moxen on turn 1 and the Viper on turn 3: one counter, Bot2 loses 4, one
# trigger (24). On turn 5 the Viper attacks: two counters, Bot2 chooses to lose 4 life both times - two triggers, each for 4
# (32) - then the Viper's 6 combat damage, a third for 6 (38). Bot2: 20 - 4 - 4 - 4 - 6 = 2.

